    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nCentrally and conveniently located in the heart of Bray, No 13 Davitt Road is a spacious and well-appointed 5 bedroom semi-detached house which is presented in an excellent condition throughout, benefitting from a rear and side extension that offers versatility with an interconnecting self-contained unit, a lovely mature landscaped rear garden with an array of planting and paved patio areas, all within a short stroll of Bray Main Street and an abundance of excellent local services and amenities.\n\nOriginally built in the 1930's as a 3-bed semi-detached house with an attached garage, the spacious and light-filled accommodation which has been modified and extended over the years currently extends to approximately 180sqm/1,938sq.ft. To the front of the house, set behind an attractive stone wall, there is private off-street parking for two vehicles on a cobble lock driveway. A very welcoming entrance hallway with smart storage under the stairs leads into the elegant front living room which has a multi-fuel stove with marble fireplace, ceiling coving and semi-solid wooden floors which are a feature throughout the downstairs. The back of the house is home to a fully equipped kitchen with a breakfast bar, a lounge area, a dining room, a guest WC, and a utility room. The open plan kitchen/lounge/dining area which incorporates a single storey is bathed in natural light via two large Velux roof lights and seamlessly connects with the outside patio and raised garden via large floor to ceiling windows with French doors. A door under the staircase leads into a 1-bed annex which has its own kitchenette, bathroom and living room with access to the rear garden it offers the opportunity for multi-generational living, the option for rental income, a space for an au pair or a separate space for those working from home. Rising upstairs there are three spacious double bedrooms (the principal bedroom which overlooks the garden comes with an ensuite), a single bedroom and a shower room.\n\nThe garden is a lovely feature with this property, measuring approximately 10m in width by 15m in length, there are two paved patio areas that are ideal for 'al fresco' dining or a nice place to sit and relax on a nice day. A central grass lawn area is surrounded by an array of mature planting that offers a lovely sense of seclusion. A partially covered side passageway offers useful storage.\n\nLocation:\nDavitt Road benefits from a unique and convenient setting in one of the best and most desirable locations that Bray has to offer, within a few minutes' walk to the Main Street & Town Centre, the DART station, and the seafront, giving future buyers the perfect mix between the convenience of an established community and the peace of seaside living. The vibrant seafront offers a range of cafes, ice cream parlours, bars & restaurants along its famous 'mile long' Victorian promenade which is a lovely place to go for a leisurely stroll and take in the coastal scenery which is framed by Bray Head at the southern end, whilst the harbour on the northern end provides a range of water activities. \n\nBray is a bustling seaside town with a vibrant community that is situated approx. 22km south of Dublin City Centre and acknowledged as the gateway to the 'garden county of Ireland'. Excellent public transport links (DART and Dublin Bus) and easy access to the N11/M11 and M50 road network provides an easy commute to Dublin, Dublin airport (40 minute drive) and beyond. Bray also offers a choice of excellent primary and secondary schools; a selection of sports and leisure facilities including golf, tennis, Bray Emmets, Shoreline and other sporting clubs; and the Mermaid Theatre with numerous arts events. Bray Town Centre is a great recent addition to the town and the area with likes of Penny's, Sports Direct, Sketchers, Butlers Café, and soon to be opened cinema. Local attractions include Kilruddery House & Gardens; the Belmont Demesne; The Powerscourt Estate with its world renowned gardens, a Distillery, Hotel and two championship golf courses; the iconic Great Sugarloaf Mountain; the Vartry Reservoir; Glendalough and more. Bray is a thriving town that offers the best of coastal, suburban and country living."
      },
